<section id="ecosystem" aria-labelledby="ecosystem-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">Local-first by design</p>
  <h2 id="ecosystem-heading">Authentication Ecosystem</h2>
  <p>Desktop-2FA is the foundation of a local-first authentication ecosystem. Its encrypted vault, cryptography and TOTP engine provide the desktop secure core; interfaces bring those capabilities to the places you use them.</p>
  <div class="ecosystem-grid">
    <article><h3>Desktop-2FA → secure core</h3><p>Available now. Manage accounts through the CLI or terminal UI, generate codes offline and create encrypted backups. You choose the vault location and control its password.</p></article>
    <article><h3>D2FA Watch → companion experience</h3><p>The first ecosystem extension. Access codes and countdowns on Wear OS with local encrypted storage and password-protected sessions. The watch can operate independently; desktop-to-watch account transfer is planned.</p><a href="#watch">Explore D2FA Watch</a></article>
    <article><h3>Future clients → planned ecosystem expansion</h3><p>Additional interfaces are planned around the same local-first architecture. Platforms, delivery dates and integration mechanisms will be announced when defined.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
